# 8.3.diagnosis.superposition.envelope.stone

## .what

state the **envelope** — the outer bounds of the whole live superposition: the worst-case across all
live scenarios (the floor the plan must be safe against) and the best-case across all (the cap the
plan must not overtreat past). this is the hand-off artifact the prescriber's phase-9 plan is built
to fit.

## .inputs

- `8.1.diagnosis.superposition.ranked.yield.md` — the ranked live scenarios + packages
- `8.2.diagnosis.superposition.eliminated.yield.md` — what was ruled out
- `7.3.acuity.envelope.watch.yield.md` — the closed acuity envelope

## .do

- state the **worst-case corner** — the most severe un-eliminated trajectory across all live
  scenarios; this is what the plan must never contraindicate against (the veto source)
- state the **best-case corner** — the most benign trajectory across all live scenarios; this is what
  the plan must not overtreat past (the no-waste bound)
- name the **no-regret core** — the care that helps across the whole envelope, harmless at both
  corners (from 6.3)
- carry the acuity floor (phase 7) so the prescriber inherits urgency + bounds together

## .emit

into `8.3.diagnosis.superposition.envelope.yield.md` — the worst/best corners, the no-regret core,
and the acuity floor.

## .done when

both envelope corners are stated, the no-regret core is named, the acuity floor is carried, and the
diagnostician's hand-off to the prescriber is complete.
